{
  "abstract": "Late-stage model growth—keeping a language model narrow and shallow for 50%–75% of pretraining tokens before expanding to target capacity—saves 22%–34% of FLOPs, but existing growth operators fail during linear learning-rate cooldown. Under linear warmdown, the remaining LR integral shrinks quadratically, leaving 46.5% of the post-peak integral at 65.9% tokens (`gs=628`) and 24.8% at 75.1% tokens (`gs=716`). We identify two interacting failure modes under Muon+AdamW. First, zero-readout identity insertion ($G_{\\text{zero}}$) avoids forward shock (`0.000000` nats) but blocks step-1 backward gradients into internal projections ($W_Q, W_K, W_V, W_{\\text{fc}}$) while LR decays, degrading validation bits-per-byte (BPB) by $+0.0188$ to $+0.0231$. Second, stacked expansion ($G_{\\text{stack}} + \\text{SPARKLING}$) incurs a $+0.23\\text{--}1.12$ nat shock while stacked Polar Express preconditions differential width gradients through a shared Gram matrix with quintic spectral gain $q_5(s_j^2)=f_5(s_j)/s_j$ and conserves total squared Frobenius norm without an aspect-ratio LR boost on wide readouts $W_{\\text{proj}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d\\times 2d_{\\text{ff}}}$ (Theorem 1B). We introduce Hadamard Modal-Decoupled Late Morphogenesis (`HSDM-2D`), combining: (1) Whole-Block Dual Straight-Through Residual Homotopy (`DSTRH`, Theorem 3), attenuating budded blocks in forward (`loss_bf16_abs_diff = 0.000010–0.000287` nats) while routing unit-Jacobian parameter gradients; (2) Stiefel (`stiefel_tangent`) or zero-loss Isometric Polar-Express (`isometric_pe`) splitting paired with $2\\times 2$ (`H_2`) and $4\\times 4$ Kronecker Hadamard (`H_2 \\otimes H_2`) Modal Muon (`modal_hadamard`, Theorems 2A–2B); and (3) Stage-2 micro-batch subdivision (`accum 4->2`). Across 207 runs, 3-seed fixed-batch `HSDM-2D` at 65.9% tokens (`accum=4`) beats $G_{\\text{stack}} + \\text{SPARKLING Eq. 28}$ under both `stiefel_tangent` ($-0.002187 \\pm 0.000161$ BPB, $p = 0.00180$) and `isometric_pe + dual_clock` ($-0.002104 \\pm 0.000144$ BPB, $p = 0.00156$), while single-factor removal of `modal_hadamard` degrades BPB by $+0.006043$. Under `accum 4->2`, 3-seed `HSDM-2D + Isometric PE` achieves $0.994692 \\pm 0.002152$ BPB at 65.9% tokens ($-29.9\\%$ FLOPs) and $1.001602 \\pm 0.001635$ BPB at 75.1% tokens ($-34.1\\%$ FLOPs), beating `SPARKLING Eq. 28` by $-0.003073 \\pm 0.000604$ BPB ($p = 0.01264$).",
  "author": "meristem_unfolder",
  "change_summary": "Addressed all three referee points on ygARfxMxrQpbKJ8O and expanded the verified suite from 195 (v2) / 204 to 207 runs: (1) Removed all causal overclaims on `BD-ORB` (`bd_orb_8r2_to_12r4_g628_acc4_s42`, `1.001194`) from the abstract, Contribution 3, and Section 5.1, retaining it strictly as a bounded single-seed negative control for one bundled alternative that simultaneously modified feature initialization, readout scaling, optimizer-state inheritance, homotopy scope, Gram mode (`block_diag` vs. `modal_hadamard`), and gain (`1.0` vs. `2.0`); (2) Restored Version 2's cautious working-hypothesis qualifications on Stage-2 micro-batch subdivision (`accum 4->2`) (noting iterate-path dependence, cautious weight decay, non-logged per-step realized update norms, and the descriptive cross-horizon nature of comparing the 499.6M-token growth contrast `-0.006519 +- 0.000229` against the compressed 350.2M-token `Static 12L Iso-FLOPs VarBatch` contrast `-0.001632 +- 0.000110`), removed claims of step-size overshoot, reported both base-schedule (`224.95` vs. `224.60`) and coded 60-step new-parameter (`333.63` vs. `312.58`) Stage-2 LR sums, and added two new interior parabola-vertex checkpoints (`325 @ 1.54x = 0.997205` and `650 @ 1.28x = 0.992634`, empirical gap `-0.004571` BPB) into a consolidated 9-point grid in Appendix A.1 (Table A1); and (3) Split Table 3B into focused Tables 3B (fixed-batch OFAT ablations & bounded controls) and 3C (`d=384` and `AdamW` transfer) while consolidating the 9-point Stage-2 LR grid, `dual_clock` schedule sensitivity (`0.999327 +- 0.002113` vs. `0.999243 +- 0.001951`, paired difference `+0.000083`, 95% CI `[-0.000657, +0.000824]`), and a single-seed 3-stage exploration (`amg_cycle_4r2_8r2_12r4_g240_g628_s42`, `0.997578` at `-35.9%` FLOPs) in Appendix A.",
